=head2 SDL_LockJoysticks

  SDL_LockJoysticks();

C: C<< void SDL_LockJoysticks(void) >>

Locking for atomic access to the joystick API.

The SDL joystick functions are thread-safe, however you can lock the joysticks while processing to guarantee that the joystick list won't change and joystick and gamepad events will not be delivered.

It is safe to call this function from any thread.

Since: This function is available since SDL 3.2.0.

=head2 SDL_UnlockJoysticks

  SDL_UnlockJoysticks();

C: C<< void SDL_UnlockJoysticks(void) >>

Unlocking for atomic access to the joystick API.

This should be called from the same thread that called SDL_LockJoysticks().

Since: This function is available since SDL 3.2.0.

