=head2 SDL_GetJoystickProperties

  my $result = SDL_GetJoystickProperties($joystick);

C: C<< SDL_PropertiesID SDL_GetJoystickProperties(SDL_Joystick * joystick) >>

Get the properties associated with a joystick.

The following read-only properties are provided by SDL:

- `SDL_PROP_JOYSTICK_CAP_MONO_LED_BOOLEAN`: true if this joystick has an LED that has adjustable brightness - `SDL_PROP_JOYSTICK_CAP_RGB_LED_BOOLEAN`: true if this joystick has an LED that has adjustable color - `SDL_PROP_JOYSTICK_CAP_PLAYER_LED_BOOLEAN`: true if this joystick has a player LED - `SDL_PROP_JOYSTICK_CAP_RUMBLE_BOOLEAN`: true if this joystick has left/right rumble - `SDL_PROP_JOYSTICK_CAP_TRIGGER_RUMBLE_BOOLEAN`: true if this joystick has simple trigger rumble

It is safe to call this function from any thread.

=over

=item joystick - SDL3::Joystick object or undef. the SDL_Joystick obtained from SDL_OpenJoystick().

=back

Returns unsigned integer: a valid property ID on success or 0 on failure; call SDL_GetError() for more information.

Since: This function is available since SDL 3.2.0.

