=head2 SDL_GetJoystickGUID

  my $result = SDL_GetJoystickGUID($joystick);

C: C<< SDL_GUID SDL_GetJoystickGUID(SDL_Joystick * joystick) >>

Get the implementation-dependent GUID for the joystick.

This function requires an open joystick.

It is safe to call this function from any thread.

=over

=item joystick - SDL3::Joystick object or undef. the SDL_Joystick obtained from SDL_OpenJoystick().

=back

Returns SDL3::GUID object: the GUID of the given joystick. If called on an invalid index, this function returns a zero GUID; call SDL_GetError() for more information.

Since: This function is available since SDL 3.2.0.

=head2 SDL_GetJoystickVendor

  my $result = SDL_GetJoystickVendor($joystick);

C: C<< Uint16 SDL_GetJoystickVendor(SDL_Joystick * joystick) >>

Get the USB vendor ID of an opened joystick, if available.

If the vendor ID isn't available this function returns 0.

It is safe to call this function from any thread.

=over

=item joystick - SDL3::Joystick object or undef. the SDL_Joystick obtained from SDL_OpenJoystick().

=back

Returns unsigned integer: the USB vendor ID of the selected joystick, or 0 if unavailable.

Since: This function is available since SDL 3.2.0.

