C: C<< void SDL_GetJoystickGUIDInfo(SDL_GUID guid, Uint16 * vendor, Uint16 * product, Uint16 * version, Uint16 * crc16) >>

Get the device information encoded in a SDL_GUID structure.

It is safe to call this function from any thread.

=over

=item guid - SDL3::GUID object. the SDL_GUID you wish to get info about.

=item vendor - reference to a scalar holding unsigned integer, pointer object or undef. a pointer filled in with the device VID, or 0 if not available.

=item product - reference to a scalar holding unsigned integer, pointer object or undef. a pointer filled in with the device PID, or 0 if not available.

=item version - reference to a scalar holding unsigned integer, pointer object or undef. a pointer filled in with the device version, or 0 if not available.

=item crc16 - reference to a scalar holding unsigned integer, pointer object or undef. a pointer filled in with a CRC used to distinguish different products with the same VID/PID, or 0 if not available.

=back

Since: This function is available since SDL 3.2.0.

