=head2 SDL_GetNumJoystickAxes

  my $result = SDL_GetNumJoystickAxes($joystick);

C: C<< int SDL_GetNumJoystickAxes(SDL_Joystick * joystick) >>

Get the number of general axis controls on a joystick.

Often, the directional pad on a game controller will either look like 4 separate buttons or a POV hat, and not axes, but all of this is up to the device and platform.

It is safe to call this function from any thread.

=over

=item joystick - SDL3::Joystick object or undef. an SDL_Joystick structure containing joystick information.

=back

Returns integer: the number of axis controls/number of axes on success or -1 on failure; call SDL_GetError() for more information.

Since: This function is available since SDL 3.2.0.

